                      "$type": "Models.Memo, Models",
                      "Text": "Koocheki et al. (2016) estimated the light extinction coefficient of sesame to be 0.681, averaged across six genotypes. The plant densities were 40 plants/m2 and inter-row spacing was 0.5m.\n\n- Koocheki, A., Nassiri Mahallati, M., Solouki, H., & Karbor, S. (2016). Evaluation of Radiation Absorption and use Efficiency in Substitution Intercropping of Sesame (Sesamum Indicum L.) and Mung Bean (Vigna Radiata L.). Advances in Plants & Agriculture Research, 3(5). https://doi.org/10.15406/apar.2016.03.00109.",
